# PART 2 — CRITICAL REPOSITORY AND APPLICATION SEPARATION

THIS IS A NON-NEGOTIABLE ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT.

Create TWO COMPLETELY SEPARATE GIT REPOSITORIES.

Do not place the Gateway and Chatbot into the same repository.

Do not use a monorepo.

Do not share application source folders between them.

Do not make the Gateway dependent on the Chatbot application.

Do not make the Chatbot dependent on the Gateway's internal implementation.

The only integration between the two systems must happen through documented public APIs, WebSocket interfaces, and a versioned protocol/SDK.

