# PART 12 — LOCAL, CLOUD AND HYBRID EXECUTION

Support different deployment models for Personal AI.

## 12.1 Local mode

The Personal AI runs on the owner's device or server.

Advantages:
- Owner-controlled execution.
- Local memory.
- Local tools.
- Greater control over data.

Requirements:
- Local runtime.
- Secure identity storage.
- Gateway connection.
- Reconnection.
- Offline state handling.
- Protected configuration.

If the device is offline, the AI cannot execute new requests.

The Gateway may queue eligible requests until reconnection or expiration.

## 12.2 Cloud mode

The Personal AI runs on a cloud-hosted node.

Requirements:
- Isolated owner environment.
- Secure secret management.
- Per-owner data separation.
- Independent AI identity.
- Resource limits.
- Monitoring.
- Deployment lifecycle.
- Backup and recovery.

## 12.3 Hybrid mode

The user can have a cloud node and local runtime working together.

Define which runtime is authoritative for identity, memory and execution.

Avoid duplicate execution and inconsistent memory.

## 12.4 Offline handling

Implement:
- Presence status.
- Queueable request types.
- Message expiry.
- Reconnection.
- Delivery retry.
- Idempotency.
- User-visible offline status.
- Explicit cloud fallback policy.

Never silently switch to a cloud execution environment if the user has selected local-only execution.

